{%- comment -%}
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONTENT FRESHNESS (custom vcollect)

Renders the visible publication / last-review line of an editorial page, and nothing else.

Why it exists: freshness is a selection criterion for generative engines, and the date they read has to be the same one
a human reads on the page. This snippet is the single renderer of that line, so the entity page, the release calendar,
the glossary and the comparison tables can never format or source it differently.

Source of the date: Shopify's Liquid `page` object exposes `published_at` but no `updated_at` (verified against
shopify.dev/docs/api/liquid/objects/page, 30/07/2026), so the review date is stored in the `vcollect.date_maj`
metafield. snippets/structured-data.liquid reads that same metafield for the dateModified of the WebPage node: one
source, no drift between the markup and the page.

When the metafield is empty, the publication date is shown and no "updated on" claim is made. A date that quietly stops
moving is worse than no date at all.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign date_modified = page.metafields.vcollect.date_maj.value
-%}

{%- if date_modified != blank -%}
  <p class="content-freshness">
    {{ 'about.last_updated' | t }}
    <time datetime="{{ date_modified | date: '%Y-%m-%d' }}">{{ date_modified | date: '%d/%m/%Y' }}</time>
  </p>
{%- elsif page.published_at != blank -%}
  <p class="content-freshness">
    {{ 'about.published_on' | t }}
    <time datetime="{{ page.published_at | date: '%Y-%m-%d' }}">{{ page.published_at | date: '%d/%m/%Y' }}</time>
  </p>
{%- endif -%}
